# Three pasted fragments in one document, each on its own path: a bare fragment
# ahead of the real block for dir/file.txt, the same fragment with a stray prose
# operation line ahead of dir/fileb.txt, and dir/filec.txt with no fragment as
# the control. A fragment is a git block that names a path and claims an
# operation but never reaches a payload, so the reader must drop it and let the
# real block further down keep the path. Both operands carry the same document,
# so all three paths must stay silent together and the report must be empty.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: patch1 patch2
exit: 0
